pendell@hotmail.com wrote:

> 1) Soldier ant.
> Reason:  There are fast animals, and strong animals. The solution is to
> fight the one and outrun the other.  But the soldier animal is both
> fast and strong, and moreover possesses a poison attack that can
> instakill you. Even if it doesn't, it can still take a couple points of
> strength which you'll miss, as in the early game you don't have a
> unicorn horn yet. Oh, and it hunts in packs.

I hardly ever see any of these, at least not until I'm well able to handle 
them.
> 
> 2) Killer bee.
> Reason: Fast, hunts in packs,  potential instakill with poison.  Tiny
> creature makes it hard to hit.

Occasionally a pain, but usually I have poison resistance long before I 
meet any of these.

> 3) Cockatrice
> Reason:  More ways to kill oneself with a cockatrice corpse than with
> just about anything else in the game. Indeed, the creature is more
> dangerous dead than alive, whether it's by smacking it when you've
> forgotten you're wearing gloves, feeling it on a square and being
> instapetrified, or touching it while falling, the cockatrice is always
> a dangerous enemy.

Dangerous to careless play certainly, and I've succumbed to the corpses 
more than once, but usually meeting a cockatrice is more of a benefit than 
a problem.

I'd say Winter wolf cubs in the earlyish game, and Titans mid game are 
worse than the above.


